WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.834
(upbeat Italian-style music)

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.084
- That's crazy.

00:00:10.503 --> 00:00:12.486
- So we just heard about this
place here in Philadelphia

00:00:12.486 --> 00:00:15.634
that sells pizza flavored ice cream.

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:18.666
The shop posted a photo on
Instagram of a scoop of the

00:00:18.666 --> 00:00:21.361
ice cream on a slice of pizza.

00:00:21.361 --> 00:00:23.754
Instagram went crazy.

00:00:23.754 --> 00:00:25.769
I figured I have to check this out.

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:28.808
Philadelphia's far,
and I don't have a car.

00:00:28.808 --> 00:00:30.928
- Come on, let's go!

00:00:30.928 --> 00:00:33.845
(electronic music)

00:00:38.278 --> 00:00:40.028
Hello Philly.

00:00:42.387 --> 00:00:46.554
- Alright, so we are just
short of Philadelphia now.

00:00:48.351 --> 00:00:52.470
We're heading to Little Baby's Ice Cream

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.887
where the have a pizza flavored ice cream

00:00:57.811 --> 00:01:01.698
that you can get on top
of a slice of pizza.

00:01:01.698 --> 00:01:03.384
- [Rob] The garlic scares me.

00:01:03.384 --> 00:01:07.096
That's an ingredient in ice
cream that I'm not quite sure--

00:01:07.096 --> 00:01:09.271
- [Christian] I bet they
put some thought into this.

00:01:09.271 --> 00:01:12.188
(electronic music)

00:01:17.711 --> 00:01:19.294
Alright, so we're not exactly sure

00:01:19.294 --> 00:01:20.841
what we're doing at the moment.

00:01:20.841 --> 00:01:21.758
- Here we go.

00:01:21.758 --> 00:01:22.739
- You see it?

00:01:22.739 --> 00:01:24.553
- It's up here on the left.

00:01:24.553 --> 00:01:28.136
(Italian-style folk music)

00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:41.021
- We're about to try their
pizza flavored ice cream.

00:01:41.021 --> 00:01:44.854
- So tomato paste ice
cream, oregano, garlic--

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.239
- And just deliciousness.

00:01:50.239 --> 00:01:53.005
There's a pizza place
that's literally connected

00:01:53.005 --> 00:01:57.870
to Little Baby's Ice Cream,
so not only are we gonna have

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:00.758
some of their pizza flavored ice cream,

00:02:00.758 --> 00:02:04.925
we're also gonna have that
on top of a slice of pizza.

00:02:07.157 --> 00:02:10.508
This is definitely one
of the stranger items

00:02:10.508 --> 00:02:11.691
that I've eaten.

00:02:11.691 --> 00:02:12.816
- It smells fantastic.

00:02:12.816 --> 00:02:15.566
- Yeah, I mean, well, it's pizza.

00:02:19.602 --> 00:02:23.629
- I mean, that definitely
tastes like pizza.

00:02:23.629 --> 00:02:25.765
- Oh my god, it's crazy!

00:02:25.765 --> 00:02:28.733
- That is incredible how
much that tastes like pizza.

00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:30.072
- It's so good!

00:02:30.072 --> 00:02:33.686
- I definitely wouldn't want
any sort of sprinkles on this.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.363
- Sprinkled with red pepper flakes.

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:37.769
- Yeah, red pepper flakes, maybe. (laughs)

00:02:37.769 --> 00:02:41.159
I would not expect that to
taste as good as it tastes.

00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:44.318
- I love the hot and the cold together.

00:02:44.318 --> 00:02:48.251
Can you imagine if they did,
like, a pizza waffle cone

00:02:48.251 --> 00:02:49.752
and put this ice cream in it?

00:02:49.752 --> 00:02:51.968
- Hmm.
- (makes exploding noise)

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:53.323
- A bit drippy.

00:02:53.323 --> 00:02:54.741
- It gets to be a little messy.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.642
It's a little bit of a challenge

00:02:57.642 --> 00:03:00.809
to experience the good things in life.

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:04.349
- And that's frozen cheese.

00:03:07.748 --> 00:03:10.713
This place has been serving
this pizza for a while.

00:03:10.713 --> 00:03:14.880
Just this week is when they
decided to blow up on Instagram.

00:03:15.733 --> 00:03:18.548
- Yeah, they said it's been six years.

00:03:18.548 --> 00:03:21.003
- This pizza slice is actually solid.

00:03:21.003 --> 00:03:22.942
This is a good piece of pizza.

00:03:22.942 --> 00:03:26.409
And the ice cream is also pretty good.

00:03:26.409 --> 00:03:29.668
I don't think you do any favors to either

00:03:29.668 --> 00:03:31.938
by eating them together.

00:03:31.938 --> 00:03:34.483
So I wanna point out that we
are two native New Yorkers

00:03:34.483 --> 00:03:38.076
who left New York for
Philadelphia to eat pizza.

00:03:38.076 --> 00:03:39.263
- Shh.

00:03:39.263 --> 00:03:42.113
- Pizza is quintessential to New York,

00:03:42.113 --> 00:03:45.560
but Philly has something
else going for it.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.060
(jazzy music)

00:03:55.122 --> 00:03:55.955
- Oh yeah.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.496
- Philadelphia.

00:03:58.496 --> 00:04:00.070
- Bye, Philadelphia.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:02.835
- Who in New York has a car?

00:04:02.835 --> 00:04:06.177
Just this guy, the only
guy that has a car.

00:04:06.177 --> 00:04:07.720
That's not why I asked you here, though.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:08.553
- [Rob] Yes, it is.

00:04:08.553 --> 00:04:09.386
- [Christian] Yeah, it is.

00:04:09.386 --> 00:04:11.483
It's 100 percent why I asked
you here, now let's go.

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:12.908
(squeaking)

